Z||000011||Cliff Pennock||01-15-2001||07:44 PM||||Thank you all for your kind words but really, I don't deserve any credit here. The real credit goes to the people who came up with the idea and to those who made/will make any donations.<P>It restores my faith a little in the kindness of people to see that so many are willing to help out a complete stranger. Too often people are looking the other way, pretending nothing ever happened. I know we can't change the world but at least we can try to set an example here.<P>Anyway, StuGood mentioned a good point in an email to me. Did we ever decide what exactly will happen with the money? Will we buy a new Fiero for him or will we donate the amount and let the family decide what to do with it?<P>What's your opinion?||||reg||1
Z||000012||Jaygee79||01-15-2001||10:47 PM||||It looks great Cliff.||||reg||1
Z||000013||stimpy||01-15-2001||11:15 PM||||My opinion is, while it is an extremely noble gesture to want to buy Anthony a new Fiero, I think that his family will have much more pressing immediate needs.  From the sound of things, Anthony sustained some consderable head trauma as a result of his injuries.  I think a Fiero parked in the driveway would be kinda cruel if Anthony can't drive. I think the money would be better spent on getting the absolute best rehab money can buy, adapting his house so he can recover at home with his family, etc. Then, God willing, after he fully recovers, he will remember the sense of community that aided him, and will be a Fiero fan for life.  I'm sure whatever settlement comes to him down the road will buy a sufficient replacement vehicle.  <BR>Whatever the consensus is, I feel that it is truely a selfless act of kindness that has been put into motion, and I applaud the peope named in your webpage Cliff. They re indeed men of action.<P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||wkayl||01-16-2001||12:29 AM||||Cliff, <BR>Looks very impressive.  I sent a question to you by e-mail pertaining to the pictures.   Let me know so I can check it out if needed.<BR>Wayne<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||Cheever2||01-16-2001||12:44 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR>Will we buy a new Fiero for him or will we donate the amount<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>As much as I'd LIKE to say buy a Fiero, it does look like that's something that can be done later if desired.  The family does know our intentions, and Anthony does know of our reaching out to him, so the gesture is already acknowledged.  The NEED is what should be addressed.  First things first.  Let's donate the money and let the family decide.  Shouldn't be up to us when we're talking about a substantial amount that could do better good than what our desires may be.  Who knows, if they end up with extra, they may indeed think of our connection with Anthony and get a Fiero.  But they know the need better than us.<P>||||reg||6
Z||000016||wkayl||01-16-2001||12:46 AM||||Well said Cheever2.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000017||Cheever2||01-16-2001||01:29 AM||||Just paraphrasing Stimpy.  Putting the same thing in my own words.<BR>||||reg||6
