Z||000021||Oreif||01-16-2001||10:17 AM||||    <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR><B>Good points, all. So there needs to be some extra text between "...got the ball rolling." and "This page is for...". I was thinking something along the lines of:<P>[b]Since we do not know if Anthony is able or willing to drive a car again, we at PFF leave it to the family to decide how the donation is spent.</B><P>Any suggestions for additions or changes to this?[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>How about: <B> Due to the extent of Anthony's injuries, We at PFF are going to let the Barber Family decide how the donation is to be used. </B><P>I do not think saying "able or willing to drive" sounds positive.<P>Cliff, I read thru thru the page again and noticed Devestating. It should be spelled "devastating". Just letting you know.<P>BTW ~ Great Job so far from everyone!<BR>Especially Cliff for the space and time to assist us!<P><BR>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 01-16-2001).]||||reg||1
